P1 closed and committed as `ce99e65e` (`fix(yang.typescript): authenticate retained-condition provenance against minted forgeries`) on branch `exception-js-r1r3`, on top of `c0114a42`. Not merged, not pushed, master untouched.

**Mechanism.** [prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1695): `js/raise-protocol` no longer writes the condition into the wrapper's own cell contents. It allocates a fresh runtime-owned companion cell holding `{:yang.call/wrapper e, :yang.call/seal js.rt/retained-seal, :yang.call/condition condition}` and stores only the companion reference on the wrapper. `js.rt/retained-seal` (:4133, also in `runtime-keys` :4293) is a cell `js/init!` allocates once per task that no definition returns, so admitted source cannot obtain it. [js/retained-condition](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1675) authenticates heap-authentic wrapper and companion, the companion's wrapper back-reference identical to the candidate, and seal identity — a minted cell cannot replicate the seal, a copied wrapper fails the back-reference, and the companion lives exactly as long as the wrapper with no registry. P2 comment narrowed at :1586 (restore-before-transfer claims delivery ordering only; suspension lifetime stays a named open obligation). Standing rulings respected: no nil-exit fallback, no constructor-protocol claim, donor tweak kept.

**Probes.** [exception_probes.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:161) and [exception_contract_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-jsr13/test/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj:59): a source-minted forgery (plus a companion-layout mimic) and a copied-metadata wrapper, each thrown through the donor's `raise_value`. Pre-fix both forwarded their conditions on all three VMs (6 failures — the executed P1 reproduction); post-fix both refuse with a fresh `:yang.call/thrown` carrying the thrown cell itself.

